// Regression (2026-07-28): a range narrowing inside a defer body (which runs at
// scope EXIT) leaked into the intervening code, eliding the fixed-array bounds
// guard (silent OOB). Fixed compiler: idx stays [9,9], auto-guard fires, main
// returns 0. Unfixed: idx proven [2,2], guard elided, garr[9]=7 OOB, returns 9.
//
// 2026-08-16: `wild()` used to `return 9;`, which find_return_range derives as
// the singleton [9,9] — so index_range_verdict now proves the access can NEVER
// be in bounds and rejects it outright. That is the right verdict for THAT
// program, but it stops this test exercising what it is for (the defer-body
// narrowing leak). Reading a mutable global keeps the index genuinely
// underivable, so the auto-guard path under test is still the one taken.
u8[4] garr;
u32 wild_seed = 9;
u32 wild() { return wild_seed; }
u32 main() {
    u32 idx = wild();
    defer { idx = 2; }
    garr[idx] = 7;
    return idx;
}
